ps://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Himmelbjerget_2005_(edit).jpg","w":795,"h":596,"ok_print":true}],"intro":{"body":"Horsens is a city in eastern Jutland with a population of around 61,000 (2021). Horsens is a port town at the end of a beautiful long shallow-water inlet. Such inlets are known as fjords in Denmark and there are several of them on the East Jutland coast. Horsens fjord is typical, with rolling hills and forests stretching all the way down to the water and making the city feel less like a coastal town. The larger city of Vejle south of Horsens also sits at the bottom of a Danish fjord. Horsens has a pedestrianised centre with historic buildings, cafés, restaurants and opportunities for specialty shopping, and the inner city is dotted with art installations.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Horsens","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Horsens","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"facts":{"population":61074,"visit_h":9}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-casa-arena-horsens","name":"CASA Arena Horsens","kind":"Landmark","lat":55.8716,"lon":9.8576,"dist_km":1.3,"rank_score":7.1,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Ac%20horsens.jpg?width=960","author":"Pathfinder77","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ac_horsens.jpg","w":1632,"h":1224,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-scandic-bygholm-park-restaurant","name":"Scandic Bygholm Park Restaurant","kind":"Park","lat":55.86486,"lon":9.82625,"dist_km":1.6,"sig":0.997,"rank_score":5.1,"resolved_by":"retyped","merged_from":["Bygholm"]},{"id":"hl-boller-slot","name":"Boller Slot","kind":"Castle","lat":55.8378,"lon":9.89711,"dist_km":3.9,"sig":2.009,"rank_score":4.0,"resolved_by":"catalogue","heritage":true,"merged_from":["Boller Slots voldgrav"]},{"id":"hl-rugballe-gronhoj","name":"Rugballe Grønhøj","kind":"Landmark","lat":55.87123,"lon":9.78717,"dist_km":4.1,"sig":2.009,"r